  "scope": [
    "Independent caller-driven MQTT5/311 in-memory session state using existing public Core allocation/atomic/mutex and MQTT codec/negotiation APIs. No Core change, new shared runtime, Engine pin, callback, credential ownership or background retry timer.",
    "Owned canonical full-topic QoS1/2 snapshots, original/auto packet identifiers, bounded active/ready/hash/bitmap state, PUBACK/PUBREC/PUBREL/PUBCOMP transitions and typed negative decisions. Connection-only aliases are removed. A selected partial PUBLISH is conservatively DUP on reconnection; successful PUBREC means only PUBREL is retried.",
    "Explicit authenticated Open/network End with generations, connection-only send-quota reset, resumed PUBREL progress, no same-connection timer retransmission, incoming QoS2 prepare/commit/rollback/dedup/release, finite elapsed-time expiry and explicit offline administrative reset.",
    "Missing local state with peer SessionPresent fails closed. MQTT5 missing-server state resets old local obligations;311 mismatch requires explicit reset/clean connection. Fixed nonempty ClientId and caller-bound broker/principal namespace; assigned-id adoption is part of subsequent integration.",
    "Immutable retained packet/frame data survive ACK, End, Reset and unique Session destruction. Logical object/byte/id reservations last through actual final references. The transport must finish/abandon selections and keep borrowed bytes alive; application delivery resources are separately owned.",
    "This does not yet attach state to existing Client factories. They continue refusing an unowned retained broker session. A test-only synchronous public Core socket driver proves state behavior on real TCP; it is not a new product transport or automatic reconnect implementation."
  ],
  "resource_contract": [
    "Create performs one fixed state allocation including copied identity, outgoing bitmap/hash and optional packed incoming map. Publish performs one xrt allocation for metadata/property slots/canonical wire and one payload copy. Codecs independently preflight Size/Write/Read; payload/text validation, metadata copying, mutexes, references and allocator internals remain real costs.",
    "ACK/Next/Sent/replay selection and prepared incoming transitions allocate no adapter objects. Source-level uncontended benchmark cycles take five model gates for QoS1 and eight for QoS2, in addition to Core allocator/atomic/lock costs; these are not total hardware synchronization counts.",
    "Default128 outgoing/64 incoming and16MiB count all logically owned bytes/objects, including physically held completed packets. MaxIncoming0/MaxOutgoing0 disable corresponding maps. Allocator headers/pools, external queues and native/caller buffers remain outside logical byte accounting.",
    "Measured x64 public config112/info88/frame64/packet-info32 on both OSes. Default benchmark fixed block with13-byte identity is27077 bytes on Windows and27149 on WSL. Peak live bytes for every payload/version/QoS are retained in benchmark facts. No Client public/private layout changes.",
    "All previous8 MQTT archive objects and139 Core archive objects per OS are byte-identical; only the new session object is added. This establishes no old compiled execution-path change in these artifacts, not zero overhead for selected state operations or production-performance acceptance."
  ],
